After watching a couple of comments about pickup go by through here (in case
anyone's interested, I leave PICKUP on, though I might take it off to go
down stairs or somesuch), I thought I'd throw in my 2 zorkmids' worth on the
matter.  I think what would be the most logical way to do it would be to make
the PICKUP option not binary, but trinary: on, off, and query (conditional?).

The on and off would be, as expected, normal.  PICKUP == query would simply
mean that when you stepped onto an area with items, it would give you the
option of picking everything up, as if you had moved onto the space with
PICKUP off and then hit ,.  Anyone else think this would be reasonable?...
